From e731197d59cd0ea9134a76892871bf99fcfd1035 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:37:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: meson: implement native SC2 digital playback

SC2 uses the TM2-revb FIFO layout with channel counts in CTRL2,
separate clock and data gates, and a burst-drain handshake at stop.
Add native match data and bindings instead of claiming an SM1 SoC.
Wire the actual powered audio bus, FRDDR A/B, optical SPDIF on H4
and TDM-C through TOHDMITX into the real DW-HDMI audio codec.
Initialize the audio MPLL rate families rather than inheriting firmware.

The native analog glue is supported, but the stock DT does not identify
the T9015 AVDD rail or physical AV-jack connections. Do not invent a
regulator or headphone amplifier. Analog board activation remains
blocked by those hardware prerequisites. Stereo digital hardware
acceptance is separate from source integration and combined build.

Change-Id: I1c665ddc35ed2adbd4401c0c781037a2225edf35
